  "world": {
   "notes": "Crumbl's 2024 franchise disclosure document: the average store took nearly $1.36 million (up 17% on 2023) and made an average net profit of $251,706, about 18%; the median, restated, was $223,236 on just over $1.3 million. Royalty 8% of gross sales plus 2% to the marketing fund; total investment $816,066 to $1,442,533. The chain had 1,059 shops at the end of 2024, slowed growth to 81-87 new stores that year, added catering, cakes and pies. Menu: six permanent flavours and four that rotate every Monday. Typical prices: a single cookie $4-5, a 4-pack $14-16, a 6-pack $22-25, a 12-cookie party box $35-49. Stores are closed on Sundays. The store, its staff, the distributor's name, the rent and the local events are invented; per-item costs are estimates consistent with the 20-25% cost of goods commonly cited for the chain.",
